  ("These feminine words can be applied to females: la trompeta = ‘trumpet’ or ‘female trumpet player’." 0.0920 0.9081 0.3980 0.4145 0.4144 0.0165 0.0034 0.4191 0.0493)
  ("1.2.10 Gender of names applied across sex boundaries" 0.0920 0.7261 0.4386 0.4594 0.4594 0.0208 0.0068 0.2915 0.0676)
  ("A female’s name applied to a male acquires masculine gender: tú eres un Margaret Thatcher ‘you’re" 0.0920 0.9082 0.4671 0.4836 0.4834 0.0165 0.0040 0.3918 0.0150)
  ("a Margaret Thatcher’ (said to a man of his right-wing political ideas). But men’s names usually" 0.0920 0.9081 0.4836 0.5001 0.5001 0.0165 0.0056 0.3529 0.0096)
  ("remain masculine: María, tú eres un Hitler con faldas ‘Maria, you’re a female Hitler’, lit. ‘Hitler with" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5001 0.5166 0.5164 0.0165 0.0039 0.4512 0.0599)
  ("skirts’." 0.0920 0.1487 0.5166 0.5331 0.5331 0.0165 nil 0.2327 0.0567)
  ("1.2.11 Nouns of invariable gender applied to either sex" 0.0920 0.7288 0.5572 0.5780 0.5780 0.0208 0.0068 0.2995 0.0676)
  ("Some common words applied to human beings do not change their gender. One says el bebé está" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5857 0.6021 0.6020 0.0165 0.0049 0.3460 0.0469)
  ("enfermo ‘the baby is ill’ whatever its sex, although la bebé or la bebe is nowadays commonly heard" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6022 0.6186 0.6185 0.0165 0.0047 0.3576 0.0642)
  ("for baby girl: una bebé muere al recibir un fármaco prescrito a su madre (El País, Sp.) ‘baby girl dies" 0.0920 0.9080 0.6187 0.6351 0.6350 0.0165 0.0058 0.2935 0.0245)
  ("after receiving drug prescribed for mother’ (la beba is heard in the Southern Cone). Some words" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6351 0.6516 0.6515 0.0165 0.0053 0.3163 0.0392)
  ("of common gender are:" 0.0920 0.2888 0.6516 0.6681 0.6681 0.0165 0.0048 0.3400 0.0169)
  ("el ángel angel" 0.1092 0.2198 0.6800 0.6965 0.6964 0.0165 0.0048 0.2807 0.0128)
  ("una calamidad calamity" 0.1092 0.3003 0.6965 0.7130 0.7129 0.0165 0.0048 0.3577 0.0300)
  ("una celebridad celebrity" 0.1092 0.3000 0.7130 0.7295 0.7294 0.0165 0.0048 0.2393 0.0300)
  ("un cerebrín genius/‘brainy’ person" 0.1092 0.4001 0.7295 0.7460 0.7459 0.0165 0.0048 0.2707 0.0214)
  ("un desastre disaster" 0.1092 0.2684 0.7460 0.7625 0.7624 0.0165 0.0048 0.2394 0.0214)
  ("un esperpento fright/weird-looking person" 0.1092 0.4665 0.7625 0.7790 0.7789 0.0165 0.0048 0.2871 0.0214)
  ("la estrella star (TV, etc.)" 0.1092 0.2991 0.7790 0.7955 0.7954 0.0165 0.0048 0.2816 0.0139)
  ("un genio genius" 0.1092 0.2385 0.7955 0.8120 0.8119 0.0165 0.0048 0.2839 0.0214)
  ("un ligue date/casual boy or girlfriend" 0.5233 0.8405 0.6800 0.6965 0.6964 0.0165 0.0048 0.2906 0.0214)
  ("una lumbrera genius" 0.5233 0.6901 0.6965 0.7130 0.7129 0.0165 0.0048 0.3013 0.0300)
  ("la pareja unmarried partner. See note 2" 0.5233 0.8461 0.7130 0.7295 0.7294 0.0165 0.0048 0.3285 0.0139)
  ("la persona person" 0.5233 0.6651 0.7295 0.7460 0.7459 0.0165 0.0048 0.2361 0.0139)
  ("el personaje character (in novels, etc.)" 0.5233 0.8302 0.7460 0.7625 0.7624 0.0165 0.0048 0.2710 0.0128)
  ("una pesadilla nightmare" 0.5233 0.7185 0.7625 0.7790 0.7789 0.0165 0.0048 0.3377 0.0300)
  ("(eres) un sol you’re wonderful/an angel" 0.5233 0.8563 0.7790 0.7955 0.7954 0.0165 0.0048 0.3083 0.0425)
  ("la víctima victim" 0.5233 0.6589 0.7955 0.8120 0.8119 0.0165 0.0048 0.3591 0.0139)
  ("and a few other masculine nouns can be used to refer to women, most of them, involving sexual" 0.0920 0.9080 0.8238 0.8403 0.8403 0.0165 0.0048 0.3623 0.0326)
  ("innuendo or comparisons with objects, cf. el pendón ‘trollop’/‘slut’ (lit. ‘pennant’, also la pendona)," 0.0920 0.9081 0.8403 0.8568 0.8567 0.0165 0.0042 0.3535 0.0824)
  ("el marimacho ‘tomboy’, etc." 0.0920 0.3153 0.8568 0.8733 0.8732 0.0165 0.0048 0.3918 0.0128)
  ("(1) Titles like Alteza ‘Highness’, Excelencia, Ilustrísima ‘Grace’ (title of bishops) and Majestad" 0.0920 0.9081 0.8855 0.9020 0.9018 0.0165 0.0087 0.3068 0.0225)
  ("‘Majesty’ are feminine, but the person addressed keeps his/her gender: Su Majestad estará cansado" 0.0920 0.9079 0.9020 0.9185 0.9184 0.0165 0.0039 0.3559 0.0774))
