  ("1.3 Group B: Gender of nouns referring to animals not included under 1.2 and to lifeless things 9" 0.1576 0.9088 0.0492 0.0683 0.0679 0.0154 0.0046 0.3586 0.0228)
  ("(1) Some fruits are masculine: el aguacate ‘avocado’ (la palta south of Ecuador), el albaricoque ‘apri-" 0.0920 0.9080 0.0832 0.0997 0.0994 0.0165 0.0042 0.3378 0.0225)
  ("cot’, el higo ‘fig’, el limón ‘lemon’, el melón ‘melon’, etc. ‘A banana’ is una banana for most Latin" 0.0920 0.9079 0.0997 0.1162 0.1161 0.0165 0.0064 0.3565 0.0355)
  ("Americans, but un plátano in some regions and in Spain. Plátano also means ‘plane-tree’ in Spain," 0.0920 0.9081 0.1162 0.1327 0.1326 0.0165 0.0046 0.3511 0.0968)
  ("so ‘banana tree’ is el plátano bananero." 0.0920 0.4040 0.1327 0.1492 0.1491 0.0165 0.0048 0.2678 0.0187)
  ("(2) ’Nuts’ in general are los frutos secos. However, in Latin America las nueces can be used" 0.0920 0.9081 0.1614 0.1778 0.1776 0.0165 0.0086 0.2797 0.0227)
  ("for ‘nuts’, cf. cuando está comprando nueces, debe elegir los tipos más populares como almendras," 0.0920 0.9079 0.1779 0.1943 0.1942 0.0163 0.0084 0.2425 0.0247)
  ("manís, pacanas y nueces de nogal (Colombian cookery book) ‘when buying nuts you should choose" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1944 0.2108 0.2107 0.0165 0.0041 0.3352 0.0524)
  ("the most popular kinds like almonds, peanuts, pecans and walnuts’. El maní = el cacahuete in" 0.0920 0.9082 0.2109 0.2273 0.2272 0.0165 0.0068 0.3078 0.0269)
  ("Spain." 0.0920 0.1454 0.2274 0.2438 0.2438 0.0165 nil 0.2192 0.0534)
  ("1.3.4 Masculine by form" 0.0920 0.3732 0.2679 0.2887 0.2887 0.0208 0.0068 0.3407 0.0541)
  ("(a) Nouns ending in -o are usually masculine: el colegio ‘school’, el libro ‘book’, el macro ‘macro’" 0.0920 0.9080 0.2964 0.3129 0.3128 0.0165 0.0059 0.3301 0.0225)
  ("(in computing), el resguardo ‘receipt’/‘payslip’ (e.g. from an ATM), el trampantojo ‘illusion’/‘trick’." 0.0920 0.9080 0.3129 0.3294 0.3293 0.0165 0.0040 0.3883 0.0232)
  ("There are a few exceptions, some of them important:" 0.0920 0.5379 0.3294 0.3459 0.3459 0.0165 0.0048 0.3677 0.0487)
