  ("The rest are masculine: Canadá, México (often Méjico in Spain); Aragón, Devon (all masc.)," 0.0920 0.9080 0.3726 0.3891 0.3890 0.0165 0.0098 0.3100 0.0324)
  ("(el) Paraguay, (el) Perú, Tennessee (masc.), Nuevo Hampshire, but Nueva Jersey. Some place" 0.0919 0.9081 0.3891 0.4056 0.4055 0.0165 0.0108 0.2936 0.0260)
  ("names include the definite article and may exceptionally be feminine, cf. las Hurdes (near" 0.0920 0.9080 0.4056 0.4221 0.4220 0.0165 0.0092 0.2798 0.0556)
  ("Salamanca, Spain). For use of the article with countries and place names, see 3.2.17. El Sáhara is" 0.0920 0.9081 0.4221 0.4386 0.4385 0.0165 0.0051 0.3327 0.0967)
  ("masculine." 0.0920 0.1843 0.4386 0.4551 0.4551 0.0165 nil 0.3373 0.0923)
  ("(1) Sentences like todo Colombia lo sabe ‘all Colombia knows it’ are however correct, especially" 0.0920 0.9080 0.4673 0.4838 0.4836 0.0165 0.0066 0.2960 0.0225)
